{:edb/db-before-t 952 :edb/db-after-t 953 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534265 50 #inst "2026-10-06T15:21:13.660Z" 13194139534265 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283050 13194139534265 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283063 13194139534265 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283053 13194139534265 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283056 13194139534265 true] [17592186115596 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534265 true] [17592186115596 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/7dc806c646f1e9f5edbfef789fbdc9dfca2745c637906bd61eccb8072440e8c0.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139534265 true] [17592186115596 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-28271.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139534265 false] [17592186115596 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={63}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+2}{3x} \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-3x & =2 \\\\ 3x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1)} \\\\ x & =0.692\\,5…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x+2=3(0.692\\,5…)+2=4.077\\,6…, \\\\ AC & =3x=3(0.692\\,5…)=2.077\\,6….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(2.077\\,6…)(4.077\\,6…) \\\\  & =4.236\\,0… \\\\  & ≈4.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283051 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1089 "q-251084" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/4572bd2ef8f6086ed80f5ac21e045e3cf2359680872a958a40d2f1e72f22d980.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1113 #uuid "2cd6b918-cdfb-5e98-9708-c8e5cdeb5894" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283050 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{9x+2}{5x-1} \\\\ 2(5x-1) & =9x+2 \\\\ 10x-2 & =9x+2 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =9x+2=9(4)+2=38, \\\\ AC & =5x-1=5(4)-1=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 38\\cdot 19 \\\\  & =361.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283052 13194139534265 true] [17592186283051 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534265 true] [17592186283051 1041 "field-1" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283051 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283052 13194139534265 true] [17592186283051 1110 #uuid "a370bfe0-43a2-5f72-bec9-1f4acd4d3b61" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283052 1034 "361" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283052 1111 #uuid "92b53a1d-6bea-5b5e-9866-21ac6b088d73" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283054 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1089 "q-251127" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/ba89c2cf139dd6251804ed0758c4edc4690463ba5ae14867549881a29736f9e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1113 #uuid "cc11a7a5-2ec3-59ea-b94f-5fb360c962b5" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283053 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13} & =\\frac{12}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{12}{12}\\cdot 13 \\\\ AB & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{13}^{2}-{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169-144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283055 13194139534265 true] [17592186283054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534265 true] [17592186283054 1041 "field-1" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283055 13194139534265 true] [17592186283054 1110 #uuid "65c19cd5-250d-5655-8297-513ad904b4fb" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283055 1034 "30" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283055 1111 #uuid "a33beaa4-824b-5dba-b98a-336924823fa6" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283057 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1089 "q-28319" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/576323c48b707bb198045ab932342e53709c7a3678282835430e506c1a9dd605.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1113 #uuid "93d460d7-5e43-5c54-8dd9-9e426b38eacb" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283056 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={45}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 6x & =5x+5 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =6x=6(5)=30, \\\\ BC & =5x+5=5(5)+5=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =450.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283058 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283059 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283060 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283061 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283062 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1041 "selection" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283061 13194139534265 true] [17592186283057 1110 #uuid "a9365dd0-5de5-5bb3-943c-7ba77bffe6ee" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283058 1034 "220" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283058 1111 #uuid "03fb56c6-13cd-5ec5-9ae0-8ab1ed3349f9" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283059 1034 "330" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283059 1111 #uuid "aa2d8101-6379-577e-bc22-ee9ef895b0fd" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283060 1034 "370" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283060 1111 #uuid "f3d80943-ed5b-5ec6-9507-ac6a43992483" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283061 1034 "450" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283061 1111 #uuid "e003695d-b7f7-5ccb-a094-11c9754522fd" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283062 1034 "250" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283062 1111 #uuid "3eb86b9e-d0b7-5dda-9419-dfb0108accaa" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283064 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1089 "q-76770" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/f1880dc62f774152ce5076a313928c0e8109ca174184704c5880891ed9243718.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1113 #uuid "1d010a52-cb85-50be-9c14-2be3fabea947" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283063 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2x+4}{6x+8} \\\\ 2(6x+8) & =5(2x+4) \\\\ 12x+16 & =10x+20 \\\\ 12x-10x & =20-16 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(2)+4=8, \\\\ AC & =6x+8=6(2)+8=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283065 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283066 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283067 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283068 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283069 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1041 "selection" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283066 13194139534265 true] [17592186283064 1110 #uuid "b0216c88-f52e-57a7-bbe9-c8632f3d014c" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283065 1034 "60" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283065 1111 #uuid "65a06be2-84de-5625-a5a8-48a204b0b1b8" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283066 1034 "80" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283066 1111 #uuid "9e2e8a65-90c6-5a17-9a6b-5c17a7b80204" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283067 1034 "120" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283067 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283067 1111 #uuid "d605baf3-7549-52a3-95de-a7fbf0494f48" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283068 1034 "45" 13194139534265 true] [17592186283068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534265 true] [17592186283068 1111 #uuid "de20898a-7e94-5